          "worked": "If $\\cos\\theta=0$, the original left-hand side is $\\sin^2\\theta=1$, so neither $90^\\circ$ nor $270^\\circ$ is a solution. Division by $\\cos^2\\theta$ therefore loses no solutions.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta}-\\frac{\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta}-2&=0\\\\\\tan^2\\theta-\\tan\\theta-2&=0\\\\(\\tan\\theta-2)(\\tan\\theta+1)&=0\\\\\\tan\\theta&=2\\quad\\text{or}\\quad-1\\end{align*}$$\nFor $\\tan\\theta=2$, the related angle is $\\alpha=\\tan^{-1}(2)$. Keep the calculator value unrounded until the final answer.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=\\alpha,\\ 180^\\circ+\\alpha\\\\\\theta&\\approx63^\\circ26',\\ 243^\\circ26'\\end{align*}$$\nFor $\\tan\\theta=-1$, the related angle is $45^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^\\circ-45^\\circ,\\ 360^\\circ-45^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=135^\\circ,\\ 315^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nThe four solutions are $63^\\circ26'$, $135^\\circ$, $243^\\circ26'$ and $315^\\circ$, with the non-exact angles rounded to the nearest minute.",
